---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is this for complete beginners?',
    answer:
      'No. FramerSchool assumes you already know enough to build something. We teach how professionals structure projects, model content and deliver client-ready sites.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to design from scratch?',
    answer:
      'No. Real client work usually starts with a template. The skill is adapting it: cutting what does not fit, rebuilding structure and shipping something a client would pay for.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What do you actually teach?',
    answer:
      'Architecture, CMS design, reusable systems, client workflows, performance, and the decisions behind every major choice while converting a template into a production site.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is this another Framer feature channel?',
    answer:
      'No. Features change. Systems thinking does not. Framer is the tool; professional website building is the subject.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container faq-inner">
    <div class="faq-intro">
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="t-h2">
        <span class="mask"><span data-reveal="mask">FAQ</span></span>
      </h2>
      <p class="t-body-m c-muted" data-reveal>Who this is for. Quick filters so you know if FramerSchool matches how you want to work.</p>
    </div>

    <ul role="list" class="faq-list" data-reveal>
      {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
        <li class="faq-item" data-faq-item>
          <h3>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="faq-trigger t-body-xl"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls={`faq-panel-${i}`}
              id={`faq-trigger-${i}`}
              data-faq-trigger
            >
              <span>{faq.question}</span>
              <span class="faq-sign t-label c-subtle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div
            class="faq-panel"
            id={`faq-panel-${i}`}
            role="region"
            aria-labelledby={`faq-trigger-${i}`}
            data-faq-panel
          >
            <div class="faq-panel-inner">
              <p class="t-body-m c-muted">{faq.answer}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
